# {{ package_name }}

Use `{{ package_name }}` to manage this project and execute its operations.

If you can run the CLI but cannot read files from this repository (e.g. a
sandbox with no filesystem access to the skill), run
`{{ package_name }} --ai` to print this document to stdout instead.

## Installation (if `{{ package_name }}` is not found on this machine)

This skill can end up on a machine (synced skills directory, dotfiles, a
fresh sandbox) before the CLI itself is installed there. If running
`{{ package_name }} --version` fails, install it — no PyPI publish required:

```bash
{% if repository_url -%}
uv tool install "git+{{ repository_url }}.git"
{%- else -%}
uv tool install "git+<this project's GitHub URL>.git"
{%- endif %}
```

This works identically on macOS, Linux and Windows. Do not attempt to
build or run this project from source unless explicitly asked to develop
it — installing the published tool is the correct path for using it.

## Discovery

Always start with:

    {{ package_name }} --help

For project state:

    {{ package_name }} status --json

For diagnostics:

    {{ package_name }} doctor --json

## Project initialization

If the current directory is not initialized:

    {{ package_name }} init --non-interactive

## Authentication

Never ask the user to paste credentials into command arguments.

Check first:

    {{ package_name }} auth status --json

If authentication is required:

    {{ package_name }} auth login

## Output

Prefer `--json` when consuming command output programmatically. Do not parse
human-readable terminal output when JSON output is available.

## Safety: destructive commands

Any command documented below as destructive/irreversible supports
`--dry-run` (preview only, no changes) and requires `--confirm` to run
non-interactively. Always:

1. Run it with `--dry-run` first and show the user what it would do.
2. Get explicit user sign-off before re-running it for real with
   `--confirm --non-interactive`.

Never chain a destructive command straight to `--confirm --non-interactive`
without a human having seen and approved the dry-run output first — that
defeats the point of the gate. (This template ships no destructive command
by default; update this section with the real ones as they're added.)

## Errors

Inspect, in this order, before retrying:

1. process exit code
2. JSON `error.code`
3. JSON `error.action`

Exit codes:

    0  Success
    1  General error
    2  Invalid arguments
    3  Authentication error
    4  Project not initialized
